---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Scope and Pricing | PostgreSQL Assessments | WalStack" description="WalStack quotes fixed-scope PostgreSQL performance investigations, upgrade-readiness reviews and validation sprints after a short fit review.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Scope and pricing" title="A clear scope and fixed quote before paid work." description="Tell me the cluster, the business problem and the decision you need to make. I will review fit, evidence and timing, then send a written scope and fee. There is no open-ended hourly commitment." primaryLabel="Request an Investigation" primaryHref="/contact?offer=investigation&from=/pricing" />
  <section><div class="container grid three">
    <div class="card price-card"><span class="kicker">01 · Core assessment</span><h2>PostgreSQL Performance Investigation</h2><p><strong>{site.investigationOffer.display}</strong></p><p>{site.investigationOffer.scope}. Client-run, read-only evidence; ranked findings, risk, validation plan, written report and review call.</p><p>Target: {site.investigationTurnaround} after usable evidence, subject to availability.</p><a class="button primary" data-track="primary_cta_click" href="/contact?offer=investigation&amp;from=/pricing">Request an Investigation</a><p><a href="/postgresql-performance-investigation">See full scope →</a></p></div>
    <div class="card price-card"><span class="kicker">02 · Upgrade decision</span><h2>PostgreSQL Upgrade Readiness Review</h2><p><strong>{site.upgradeOffer.display}</strong></p><p>{site.upgradeOffer.scope}. Version and extension compatibility, representative baseline, critical plan checks, blockers, go/no-go and rollback criteria, written report and review call.</p><a class="button" href="/contact?offer=upgrade&amp;from=/pricing">Ask about upgrade readiness</a><p><a href="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness">See full scope →</a></p></div>
    <div class="card price-card"><span class="kicker">03 · After qualification</span><h2>Remediation or Migration Validation Sprint</h2><p><strong>{site.sprintOffer.display}</strong></p><p>{site.sprintOffer.scope}. Agreed environments, acceptance criteria and before/after measurement. Client owns production operations. Available only after qualification.</p><a class="button" href="/contact?offer=sprint&amp;from=/pricing">Discuss a sprint</a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section><div class="container prose">
    <h2>Which review fits?</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Your decision</th><th>Start here</th><th>What you receive</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Why is latency, contention or database cost changing?</td><td><a href="/postgresql-performance-investigation">Performance investigation</a></td><td>Ranked causes, uncertainty and safe validation steps</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Can we move to a target PostgreSQL version safely?</td><td><a href="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness">Upgrade readiness</a></td><td>Blockers, baseline, go/no-go and rollback criteria</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Did a specific agreed change meet its target?</td><td>Validation sprint after qualification</td><td>Before/after measures against acceptance criteria</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <h2>How the quote is set</h2><p>I scope one cluster and one dominant workload or upgrade path first. The quote states evidence required, deliverables, exclusions, review time and the delivery window. Additional clusters, unrelated workloads or implementation need a separate scope. Advisory is available for existing clients or qualified buyers after an assessment.</p>
    <ol><li>Send the symptom or upgrade decision through <a href="/contact">the inquiry form</a>.</li><li>I review fit, evidence and timing, then send a written scope and fixed fee.</li><li>After acceptance, your team shares reviewed evidence and I deliver the report and review call.</li></ol>
    <h2>What your team owns</h2><p>Your team reviews and runs evidence collection, approves access and data handling, and executes production changes. WalStack does not include emergency response, 24×7 support or unlimited DBA staffing. A report may conclude that the evidence does not support a clear change; it will name the uncertainty and next test.</p>
    <h2>Legacy inquiries</h2><p>If you came here for a single-query review or hourly help, <a href="/contact?offer=other&amp;from=/pricing">describe the decision you need to make</a>. I will say whether a bounded assessment fits or suggest another route.</p>
    <p><a href="/sample-report">See a synthetic performance report</a> or <a href="/sample-upgrade-readiness-report">synthetic upgrade-readiness report</a> before asking for a quote.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
